{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>If his offering is a burnt offering.</b> A particularization, and the rest is explicit." "<b>From the cattle.</b> Large or small, after eight days. And because the burnt offering is brought entirely to the Most High, it is of the chosen, and the male is chosen over the female; therefore there is no female in the burnt offering." "<b>Without blemish.</b> With no defect. And after it says 'he shall offer it,' it explains — to the place where he shall offer it, for it enters into the court of the Tent of Meeting." "<b>Before HaShem.</b> Joined in meaning with 'to the entrance of the Tent of Meeting he shall offer it.'" "<b>For his acceptance before HaShem.</b> That he shall offer it willingly, and not under compulsion."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:23.553329815Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}